Instead of going to all the trouble of byte editing the save file,
why not just use "nethack -uwizard -D" to enter debug mode?

The ^W debug mode command will let you have as many wishes as you
want, and you don't even have to cheat.  There are other debug mode
commands to play with, too, like ^V to teleport to any level.  And the
"Die? [yn]" prompt will let you play forever, or at least until you
lose interest (if you find it too pointless not to be able to die,
just answer yes).

If you must have your score in the top ten list to make the game
worthwhile, just use any text editor to copy the last line from
"logfile" into the appropriate slot in "record".  While you're at it,
give yourself any score you want!  It's your game!

